@tradition lap-of-the-wren
// Lap of the Wren (0.60.7): a slow walk round the promenade together, chatting. The easiest tradition to join.
// Lantern walk (once a year, the same Monday evening, the same promenade) is rarer, so on its night it takes the place.
k: 442
title: Lap of the Wren
when: weekly monday
at: 20:30-21:15
min: 20
jitter: 10
venue: plaza
where: 3 room Promenade: bench
where: 3 room Lift plaza: bench
hold: none
who: window-seat 50%, lingers-at-meals 35%, early-to-bed 10%, everyone 22%
anim: talk
from: The promenade

== mail
- Lap of the Wren tomorrow, {time}: a slow walk round the promenade with whoever's there. No pace, no finish line.

== ask
- Lap of the Wren tonight. It's a walk. Even I can do a walk.   #funny
- Come round the promenade later? Slow lap, good company.   #warm
- Lap of the Wren at half eight. Best way to end a Monday.

== here
- Slowly. The stars aren't going anywhere.   #warm
- Once round, then tea. That's the whole plan.
- You can see the garden lights from this side.

== thanks
- You fall in with the walkers on the promenade. Nobody hurries, and the talk drifts from the week to home.   #warm

== chatter
- Lap of the Wren is the only exercise I'll admit to.   #funny
- Monday's lap is the best talk of the week. Nobody has anywhere to be.   #warm
